  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a9ec7a1e-2518-4c79-b88e-e38702c0c2f1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### The results for this model are clear. Model classified 0 value as 4. The best C_value is about 0.0007 which suggests that model is very basic. I assume that It this logistic regression approach is too primitive for this problem."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3d684960-6b3b-4c41-bbab-9ee6daaa7b1f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### I will check this out and try to do this with linear regression approach."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "61e87521-7318-419f-a18a-96d952bd7cf6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "reg_pipe = Pipeline([\n",
    "    (\"scaler\", StandardScaler()),\n",
    "    (\"regressor\", RidgeCV(cv=5))\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "reg_pipe.fit(X_train, Y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "Y_pred_cont = reg_pipe.predict(X_test)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fa1ea084-e66f-435d-8d29-cdd442b48aeb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## I will make customized treshold, because the last Y value which suggests that the patients is very sick is the least likely to have and we want to increase our overall performance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "6d5c225e-d734-4869-b701-49b39ca490cb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Accuracy after regression: 55.98%\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def apply_custom_thresholds(y_cont):\n",
    "    conditions = [\n",
    "        (y_cont <= 0.5),                         \n",
    "        (y_cont > 0.5) & (y_cont <= 1.5),\n",
    "        (y_cont > 1.5) & (y_cont <= 2.5),\n",
    "        (y_cont > 2.5) & (y_cont <= 3.8),     \n",
    "        (y_cont > 3.8)               \n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    choices = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]\n",
    "    return np.select(conditions, choices, default=2)\n",
    "\n",
    "Y_pred_reg = apply_custom_thresholds(Y_pred_cont)\n",
    "\n",
    "results_lin_reg = accuracy_score(Y_test, Y_pred_reg)\n",
    "print(f\"Accuracy after regression: {results_lin_reg:.2%}\")"
   ]
  },
